<%# The palette's body, fetched into its frame the first time ":" is pressed.

    Two lists, because there are two questions: where do I want to be, and
    which form do I want to fill out. Above them sit the two kinds of answer
    that are neither: a reference number resolves to one submission, and a
    command does something rather than opening anything. Destinations come
    first among the lists — a search that can reach every app's sidebar is the
    reason the palette exists, and "go there" is the more common ask.

    Filtering is sidebar_search_controller — the same matching, ranking and
    highlighting the sidebar's box does, over the same catalog. Only the
    surface differs, so the palette adds no search logic of its own; what it
    does add is the keyboard, which command_palette_controller owns from the
    layout above.

    `target: "_top"` on the frame is repeated here for the same reason it is
    set on the placeholder in shared/_command_palette: a result has to leave
    the frame or Turbo answers it with "Content missing". %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "command_palette", target: "_top" do %>
  <div class="pb-palette" data-controller="sidebar-search">
    <input type="text"
           class="pb-palette__input"
           autocomplete="off"
           aria-label="Search the whole system"
           placeholder="Go anywhere, open any form, jump to PLS-845 — or ask who am i"
           data-sidebar-search-target="input"
           data-command-palette-target="input"
           data-action="input->sidebar-search#filter
                        input->command-palette#resetCursor
                        keydown.enter->command-palette#activate
                        keydown.down->command-palette#next
                        keydown.up->command-palette#previous" />

    <%= render "shared/search_reference", row_class: "pb-palette__row pb-palette__row--reference" %>
    <%= render "shared/search_commands", row_class: "pb-palette__row pb-palette__row--command" %>

    <div class="pb-palette__results">
      <div class="pb-palette__section" data-sidebar-search-target="destinationsList">
        <p class="pb-palette__section-label">Go to</p>
        <% @navigation.destinations.each do |destination| %>
          <%= link_to destination.path,
                      class: "pb-palette__row",
                      target: ("_blank" if destination.external),
                      rel: ("noopener" if destination.external),
                      data: { sidebar_search_target: "destination",
                              original_name: destination.label,
                              context: destination.app,
                              keywords: destination.keywords } do %>
            <span class="search-context"><%= destination.app %></span><%= destination.label %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-palette__section" data-sidebar-search-target="formsList">
        <p class="pb-palette__section-label">Open a form</p>
        <% @catalog.forms.each do |label, path| %>
          <%= link_to label, path, class: "pb-palette__row",
              data: @catalog.search_data(label).merge(sidebar_search_target: "formLink") %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <p class="pb-palette__empty" data-sidebar-search-target="emptyState" hidden>
        Nothing matches.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
